                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eaebead1-a853-372e-a105-44f38b750c07",
                        "entry_id": "a67003ad-e26f-3d99-9231-88a4d37d7d4a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A man who serves as one of a number of attendants to a bridegroom at a wedding, one of whom is the best man."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6cb29257-046b-4e9e-b1ee-bacd53e68c73",
                                "sense_id": "eaebead1-a853-372e-a105-44f38b750c07",
                                "text": "The Scotchman, who assisted as groomsman, was of course the only one present, beyond the chief actors, who knew the true situation of the contracting parties."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "630160cd-d8b4-4a85-8e93-40c5ce494fd6",
                                "sense_id": "eaebead1-a853-372e-a105-44f38b750c07",
                                "text": "1888, Horatio Alger, The Errand Boy, Chapter XIV: Consulting the Oracle,\n\"Philip,\" said Mr. Wilbur, \"when I marry, I want you to stand up with me--to be my groomsman.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e4424d5c-fecc-48b4-9e3f-1e8d77b8d8dc",
                                "sense_id": "eaebead1-a853-372e-a105-44f38b750c07",
                                "text": "There were eight bridesmaids and groomsmen, and I asked McClellan and Franklin to be of the number, but distant service prevented them from coming, and Burnside and Reno, of the Ordnance, took their places."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
